From: TB371FC entry reconstruction study
Subject: [PATCH] bpf: provide a blinding-disabled stub when JIT is absent

Base: tem423/android_kernel_lenovo_tb371fc
      9d8abebf4ac4d45cf4cc11b5b6bc5e4483d10fd1

The backported verifier unconditionally calls bpf_jit_blinding_enabled(),
but filter.h defines it only in the CONFIG_BPF_JIT branch. The standalone
entry config (MODULES=n, BPF_JIT=n) exposed the missing declaration during
the real Clang 10 build. Blinding cannot be enabled without a JIT, so supply
the corresponding false-valued stub alongside the other non-JIT stubs.
This preserves verifier checks and does not suppress compiler diagnostics.

--- a/include/linux/filter.h
+++ b/include/linux/filter.h
@@ -1184,6 +1184,11 @@
 	bpf_prog_unlock_free(fp);
 }
 
+static inline bool bpf_jit_blinding_enabled(struct bpf_prog *prog)
+{
+	return false;
+}
+
 static inline bool bpf_jit_kallsyms_enabled(void)
 {
 	return false;
